interface.longDescription:
Tule gives your AI agent its own engineering computer. Each project is a Linux machine with OpenCascade, Tule's Python modeling API, meshers, FEA and topology optimization installed. A web viewer shows what the agent builds, live.

Ask for a part, such as "a wall hook for my bike, 3D printable". Your agent creates a Tule project, writes the model in Python, renders and checks it itself, and sends you a viewer link. You can rotate the model, open sections and download a print-ready 3MF plate for Bambu Studio, OrcaSlicer or PrusaSlicer. Projects are saved in git, so you can come back and iterate.

With this plugin your agent can:
- create, rename, save and delete projects;
- start and stop machines: Tule cloud CPUs, GPUs on your own RunPod account, or your own computer;
- list each project's outputs with viewer links, and restore earlier autosaves;
- manage SSH and API keys for working on the machine.

The modeling itself runs on the machine through the tule CLI or SSH, which the plugin sets up. It works best in Codex and other agents that can run commands; in a ChatGPT conversation the plugin manages projects and machines and shows results.

You can try it without an account. Sign in with Google to keep your projects. GPU machines are billed by RunPod to your own RunPod account; Tule never charges you.
